SJc8AAAABUbu72A","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-14T15:14:27Z","updated_at":"2026-09-14T15:14:27Z","body":"> I also checked on Wayland, which doesn't include the change from https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/75489, but it seems not to exhibit https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101357 neither with or without this PR. Maybe screen_get_usable_rect().size and screen_get_size() return the same value on Wayland? This may actually be a bug @deralmas?\r\n\r\nYes and no. On Wayland the concept of a \"screen\" is almost useless and as such there's no way to implement it properly. We can query the _window_'s usable rect though. This is yet another case where I wish that almost all `screen_*` APIs had a preferred `window_*` equivalent.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5666225112/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/